-- title:
--   Tangent inclusion preserves the first differential ideal of an algebraic subgroup
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a Philippon base field (the complex numbers or the completed algebraic closure of a $p$-adic field), let $G$ be an embedded commutative algebraic group product, let $A$ be a parametrized analytic subgroup, and let $H$ be a closed algebraic subgroup of $G$. Write $I(H)$ for the multihomogeneous vanishing ideal of $H$. Suppose every parameter direction of $A$ annihilates the differentials at the identity of the equations in $I(H)$; equivalently, the tangent kernel of $H$ along $A$ is the full parameter space.
--
--   For any polynomial translation atlas at the identity, the retained ideal generated by the translated equations in $I(H)$ and their derivatives of order at most one satisfies
--
--   $$\partial^1_{0,A} I(H)=I(H).$$
--
--   The retention operation means intersection of the contractions of the corresponding localized ideals at all nonzero homogeneous representatives of points of $G$.
--
--   This is an auxiliary first-order ideal-stability statement, not a separately numbered theorem in Philippon's paper. It isolates the algebraic step in proving local containment from tangent inclusion. Together with the composition law for differential ideals, this identity separates the first-order algebraic obligation from the higher-order analytic argument.
-- source:
--   Auxiliary lemma for Philippon, Lemmes de zeros dans les groupes algebriques commutatifs, BSMF 114 (1986), pp. 355-383: Definition 4.2 and Proposition 4.3, pp. 373-374; tangent/exponential discussion before Lemma 4.6, pp. 377-378. https://www.numdam.org/article/BSMF_1986__114__355_0.pdf

import Definitions.Def_PhilipponMultiplicity_SectionFour
set_option autoImplicit false
open PhilipponMultiplicity

theorem PhilipponMultiplicity.first_prolongation_preserves_subgroup_vanishingIdeal
    (K : Type*) [NontriviallyNormedField K] (hK : IsPhilipponBaseField K)
    (G : EmbeddedGroupProduct K) (A : AnalyticSubgroup G) (H : AlgebraicSubgroup G)
    (htangent : A.tangentKernel H.carrier = ⊤)
    (atlas : TranslationAtlas A (0 : G.Point)) :
    retainedPolynomialOperatorIdeal atlas 1 (G.vanishingIdeal H.carrier) =
      G.vanishingIdeal H.carrier := by sorry
